WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.660
Angela, Angela.

9
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.840
Today is Jim and Pam's wedding day.

10
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.100
And we are celebrating.

11
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.060
Cheers.

12
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.560
That's my drink.

13
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.520
Can you hear it?

14
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.640
I sure can.

15
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.300
Jen, I'm taking a picture of you.

16
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.200
Okay.

17
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:46.240
Well, if you take a picture, we can post this on Office Ladies Pod because I'm drinking out of a very special champagne flute.

18
00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:47.880
Tell them all about it.

19
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.800
It is, Jenna, can I say it's craptastic?

20
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.720
It is the kitschiest thing you've ever seen in your life.

21
00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:03.300
It is a champagne flute, but the stem is a series of four glass hearts.

22
00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.760
That are, like, hollow in the middle.

23
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:07.520
Yes.

24
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.620
And it's a very large champagne flute.

25
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.400
I didn't have any champagne, so I'm actually drinking an old-fashioned out of it.

26
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.360
Is that weird?

27
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.460
I think it's flippin' perfect.

28
00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:18.500
Thank you.

29
00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.080
Cheers to you.

30
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.940
I wish we were in the same room today.

31
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:21.680
Dang it.

32
00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:22.660
I know.

33
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.120
You've got a glass of red wine, though, so.

34
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.940
I came to Airwolf today.

35
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.400
I said, Sam, Jenna is pouring an old-fashioned into her Niagara champagne flute.

36
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.300
What do we got here?

37
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.280
And he goes, I think there's some stuff over there.

38
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.820
I found a bottle of red wine and a croissant.

39
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:39.880
Oh.

40
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.260
So I'm feeling very fancy.

41
00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.880
You're very European, I think, red wine and a croissant.

42
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.580
I feel like I am.

43
00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.880
Well, let me tell you where I got this champagne flute.

44
00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:59.300
When we traveled to Niagara Falls to shoot this episode, the hotel put a basket in my hotel room

45
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:08.320
with these two champagne flutes, champagne, chocolates, candies, nuts, like a whole welcome

46
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.320
basket, and they were just so delighted that the office had come to shoot there, and I was

47
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.160
so charmed by that.

48
00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.780
I thought it was the sweetest gesture, and so I ate all the food.

49
00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.280
I actually shared it with the hair and makeup ladies, and I took the champagne glasses home,

50
00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.360
and now here they are in all their glory.

51
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:28.540
Yum.

52
00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.960
Jenna, I love this story so much.

53
00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.300
You are truly my BFF, because I would have done the same thing.

54
00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.880
I would have been like, these glasses are going home with me.

55
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.160
Oh, yeah, lady.

56
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.200
I wrapped these up in a t-shirt, and I packed them in my suitcase.

57
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.160
It's amazing.

58
00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.300
We have to post it in stories.

59
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.820
You guys, Niagara Part 2, we're here to break it down for you.

60
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:47.760
That's right.

61
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.980
This is Season 6, Episode 5.

62
00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.720
It was written by Greg Daniels and Mindy Kaling and directed by Paul Feig.

63
00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.280
Let me give you a summary of what we'll be going over today.

64
00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:05.140
Last night, Andy slept on Pam's floor, because he was recovering from his torn scrotum.

65
00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.440
Michael slept by the vending machines.

66
00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.280
Dwight hooked up with Pam's friend.

67
00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.700
And Kevin is about to lose his shoes.

68
00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.480
How's that for, like, a headline?

69
00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:20.400
That's good.

70
00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:26.260
The wedding, which is happening today, is becoming even more hectic than enjoyable for Pam and Jim,

71
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.320
and ultimately, they're going to take matters into their own hands.

72
00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.260
Meanwhile, Michael makes an unlikely love connection,

73
00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.680
and the office gang surprised Jim and Pam with a celebratory dance.

74
00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.160
I love this episode so much.

75
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.900
I know we both have said that, but this second part of Niagara is when all the, like, heartstrings are pulled.

76
00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.940
I mean, it's so beautiful and cringey.

77
00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:50.820
It's fantastic.

78
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.460
We had Greg Daniels on for Niagara Part 1.

79
00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.380
We talked about the whole entire episode.

80
00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.440
So if you guys haven't heard that interview, listen to it.

81
00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.320
Now we're going to break down the second part.

82
00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.980
We have lots of fun stuff to share.

83
00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:08.160
This second part of Niagara also features the part where Jim and Pam sneak off

84
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.760
and have a wedding ceremony on Maid of the MiSt.

85
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.440
That is my fastback number one.

86
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.560
We got a fan question from Ashlyn M.

87
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:17.640
in Windsor, Canada.

88
00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:23.060
Did everyone get to go on location to Niagara Falls, or was it just Jenna and John?

89
00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:28.120
Did you stay on the American side, or did you get to go to the Canadian side as well?

90
00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.860
Well, like we said last week, Ashlyn,

91
00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:39.180
and we shot the rehearsal dinner and the church wedding and the bulk of this episode in Los Angeles.

92
00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:46.420
The only people who went to Niagara Falls were me, John Krasinski, Mindy, Randy Cordray,

93
00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:50.240
who was our line producer, our cinematographer, Randall Einhorn,

94
00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.720
our director, Paul Feig, and then a handful of crew members.

95
00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.680
And we went to the American side of Niagara Falls.

96
00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.500
And we only had, Angela, one day to shoot.

97
00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:03.680
One day.

98
00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.200
One day to get all of that?

99
00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:06.040
Yes.

100
00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.420
And I'm going to tell you now a little bit about how it all went down,

101
00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.220
because Randy had to do an insane amount of preparation to get us there.

102
00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.260
He sure did.

103
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.680
And he shared with us, you guys.

104
00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:16.940
We're going to break it down for you.

105
00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.680
You know, originally, the network said that they wanted John and I

106
00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.440
to shoot this on a green screen at, like, a fake water tank

107
00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.760
on, like, a fakie boat in Los Angeles.

108
00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:30.440
Boo!

109
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.120
Boo!

110
00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.040
Right?

111
00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:32.780
Yeah.

112
00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.140
Randy was like, no, no.

113
00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:37.220
So.

114
00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:38.560
Good for Randy.

115
00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:39.480
Yeah.

116
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.960
So Randy set out to create a budget that the network would approve

117
00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.820
for me and John to actually go.

118
00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:50.700
Now, Greg told Randy that he would like us to shoot on the Canadian side

119
00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.600
of the falls, because that's the side that has all the fun,

120
00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.180
kind of kitschy wax museums and the water park.

121
00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.240
And it had the look that Greg was going for.

122
00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.740
On the Canadian side?

123
00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.240
On the Canadian side.

124
00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:05.720
Okay.

125
00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:10.460
But Randy found out that Canada has this very strict

126
00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.460
one-for-one staffing rule.

127
00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.660
And what that means is, for every person that he brought

128
00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:21.180
from our crew, he would have to hire a Canadian to do a job.

129
00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.920
So if we wanted to bring our regular makeup artist,

130
00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.840
we would have to hire someone locally, you know,

131
00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:27.760
for a different job.

132
00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.420
It didn't have to be another makeup artist,

133
00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:33.160
but just there had to be, like, a one-for-one representation

134
00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.000
on this crew.

135
00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:36.020
Oh.

136
00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.980
We did not have the budget for that.

137
00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:38.720
Got it.

138
00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.820
He also said that Canada has a 14-day embargo on all equipment.

139
00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.120
So any costumes, cameras, props, we would have to send it 14 days

140
00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:49.820
ahead of time.

141
00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.260
Well, we couldn't do that because we were using all that stuff

142
00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.360
in Los Angeles.

143
00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.100
Right.

144
00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.100
So Randy got this approved.

145
00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:58.840
Great.

146
00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.340
We had the budget to shoot on the American side of the falls.

147
00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.300
But then there was a problem.

148
00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.720
The Maid of the Mist, it's in, like, dual waters.

149
00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.520
Also, the Maid of the Mist is owned by a Canadian company.

150
00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.000
So that was a whole thing that Randy had to work out.

151
00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:16.980
That's right.

152
00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:21.540
Because he said they leave Canada and then cross over into American waters.

153
00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:22.080
Yes.

154
00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.440
But then they go back to Canada.

155
00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:24.320
Right.

156
00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.960
But then they do have a boat that will start on the American side

157
00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.860
or will pick up Americans and go back to the Canadian side.

158
00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:38.920
So you can ride it from the American side, but there's limited access to those rides.

159
00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.300
Most of the rides start on the Canadian side.

160
00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.520
It was a whole thing.

161
00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:45.000
This is so complicated for a boat ride.

162
00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:51.980
I mean, while I was in my hotel room with my fancy champagne glasses,

163
00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:57.240
I had no idea everything that had gone on to get me there to that gift basket.

164
00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:57.840
Wow.

165
00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:03.880
Randy shared with us that there were a lot of people that made this amazing moment happen for Jim and Pam.

166
00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.580
We promised him we would give them a shout out.

167
00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:11.500
He said, first, he was in touch with the film commissioner there, Tim Clark.

168
00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.840
Randy described him as a fountain of resources.

169
00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.620
Tim put Randy in touch with the location manager, Michelle Barone.

170
00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.360
Randy was also in touch with Tim Ruddy.

171
00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:25.580
He was the vice president of marketing for the Maid of the Miss Steamboat Company.

172
00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:29.180
Angela Birdie, the media director of Niagara State Park.

173
00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:33.000
She was a huge fan of the show, and Randy said she helped a lot.

174
00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:37.360
Randy even had to write a proposal to the New York governor's office,

175
00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:42.040
and there was a film liaison there named Pat Kaufman who helped Randy get it all done.

176
00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:47.240
He said this was the nicest group of people, and they just really made it happen.

177
00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.940
Without them, this scene would not have happened.

178
00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:50.980
Wow.

179
00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:57.220
Well, listen, I have even more stories to tell about our adventures getting on this boat.

180
00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:01.040
I'll save them for the breakdown, but it was incredible.

181
00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:09.660
So let's move on to fast fact number two, which is a follow-up on that horse going over the falls

182
00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:14.220
deleted storyline that Greg told us about in his interview last week.

183
00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:14.980
Remember that?

184
00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.520
Not only do I remember, I'm so excited.

185
00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:23.280
I brought the table draft script to our recording session so I could read the scene.

186
00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:23.860
What?

187
00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:24.780
Yes.

188
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.800
Oh, my gosh.

189
00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:26.380
This is perfect.

190
00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:30.320
I was just going to say, do you want to remind people what the story was?

191
00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.220
But you have it.

192
00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:32.180
You have it.

193
00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.500
I have it.

194
00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.520
I have what we read at the table read.

195
00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:36.780
Oh, my God.

196
00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.560
This is an exclusive.

197
00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:39.660
Okay.

198
00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:40.440
Here it goes.

199
00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:45.400
So in the table draft, Jim and Pam are saying their wedding vows.

200
00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:50.460
Jim is saying, in joy and in sorrow, in sickness and in health, as long as we both shall live,

201
00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.620
suddenly gasps race through the audience.

202
00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.760
The minister looks up and stops.

203
00:09:57.020 --> 00:10:02.660
The camera whips over to see a man leading a horse into the space.

204
00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:06.080
On top of the horse is Roy, dressed in a suit.

205
00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:10.040
I have to point out, Roy didn't even ride the horse into the church.

206
00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.660
He had, like, a guy bring him in?

207
00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:14.080
He has a guy leading him.

208
00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:17.280
Like, someone is holding the reins, walking him in.

209
00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:19.380
Roy yells, wait.

210
00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.760
Pam has a horrified expression.

211
00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:28.220
Everyone is staring, shocked at Roy, who tries to keep the horse pointed at Pam.

212
00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:31.580
But the handler struggles to keep it pointed the right way.

213
00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:34.620
So, like, Roy has no command over this horse at all.

214
00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.820
The horse's tail whips by Stanley's face, who looks annoyed.

215
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:43.300
Jim whispers to himself, holy f***.

216
00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:44.260
What?

217
00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.980
They had an F-bomb?

218
00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.260
They had an F-bomb.

219
00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:55.440
Roy says, Pammy, we lived together for nine years and did everything a man and wife do.

220
00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.540
Camera pans over to Meemaw.

221
00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:01.300
Pam is horribly uncomfortable.

222
00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:09.160
Roy, you loved me once, and can you imagine ever seeing me again as your knight on a white horse or a brown horse?

223
00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:11.240
People change, and I have, too.

224
00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.880
If you have any second thoughts, any at all, don't do this thing.

225
00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.400
Pam, I don't have any second thoughts, Roy.

226
00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:20.720
I love Jim, not you.

227
00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.940
I wish you had just called firSt.

228
00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.840
Long, awkward pause.

229
00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:31.800
Then Roy says, then I will leave you with this thought.

230
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.300
You're making a mistake.

231
00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:35.960
Jim, seriously, man?

232
00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.180
Roy, get me out of here.

233
00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:40.960
That's what he says to the handler of the horse.

234
00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.140
Jim, you could have learned to ride it, you know.

235
00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.600
That would have been a little less.

236
00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.300
And then Pam goes, Jim, Jim, Jim.

237
00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:52.180
The handler walks the horse away as Roy tries to keep his dignity.

238
00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:54.580
Oscar Booth, boo.

239
00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:59.560
And then the minister says, okay, where were we?

240
00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:04.360
He starts them back into their vows, but the camera pans over to Dwight.

241
00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:10.340
Dwight is seated next to a wedding guest and says, that is a powerful-looking horse.

242
00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.020
Excuse me.

243
00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:12.320
He gets an idea.

244
00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.740
He gets up and follows Roy out.

245
00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:16.320
Wow.

246
00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:18.060
Wow.

247
00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:18.740
Yeah.

248
00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.440
And then the other scenes are the ones Greg talked about, where Dwight convinces Roy to

249
00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:23.760
let him return the horse.

250
00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:29.380
But then, because he's seen all of this, like, historical footage of animals that can go

251
00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:33.920
over the falls and survive, Dwight then tries to ride the horse over the falls, but then

252
00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:34.500
he bails.

253
00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.200
EMS, like, rescues Dwight.

254
00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:39.100
But the horse goes over, but the horse survives.

255
00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:40.460
Yeah.

256
00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:45.840
It was a crazy storyline, and Greg shared that they did end up cutting this.

257
00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:51.180
But one thing Greg said in his interview really piqued my curiosity.

258
00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:56.620
I mean, there were so many things, but he said that, you know, this storyline wasn't cut until

259
00:12:56.620 --> 00:13:00.240
the table read, which is about one week before we started shooting.

260
00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:01.320
Oh, yeah.

261
00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:07.340
So we were very close to shooting, and this entire time, Randy had been prepping this episode

262
00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.840
as if a horse was going to go over the falls.

263
00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:16.820
And Greg even said, like, they went to Universal Studios and they saw a demonstration of a water

264
00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:20.520
tank and how the horse might fall into the water tank.

265
00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.640
And I was like, what?

266
00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.740
So I reached out to Randy Cordray.

267
00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:32.100
Angela, I have to share with you how much prep he did on this horse scene that was cut.

268
00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:33.680
I find it fascinating.

269
00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:41.120
I still can't get over the fact that this horse story was a go until about seven days before we shot.

270
00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.100
I know.

271
00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:43.220
All right.

272
00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:46.580
Here's the first thing that Randy said to me, and I'm going to quote him.

273
00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:52.200
He said, I had never been asked to create a scene of such complexity and magnitude.

274
00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:58.520
This was far beyond the scope of creating the rainy proposal rest stop or throwing a fake

275
00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:04.280
cat into the ceiling or adding a soccer ball careening off of Phyllis's head or producing

276
00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.820
a Cloris Leachman Jack Black mini movie.

277
00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:14.100
I was fearful that our meager television budget was far too small to produce the needed quality

278
00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:17.280
to make this gag appear credible and above all funny.

279
00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:23.760
But he said, nonetheless, he moved forward as that was what he had to do.

280
00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:32.880
So he said, the first thing he had to do was find a church in Los Angeles that could fit a horse

281
00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.020
through its front doors.

282
00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.740
That's how we picked the church?

283
00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:41.000
Yeah, because Roy had to come in riding a horse.

284
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:47.240
So not just big enough to fit a horse, but fit a man on a horse through the front doors.

285
00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.600
And I guess a man leading a horse.

286
00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:53.220
Imagine that, Scout.

287
00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:55.080
Imagine that.

288
00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.820
Are you just measuring church doors?

289
00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.700
And then the people are like, what are you measuring for?

290
00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:04.560
This makes the church choice make sense to me now because it was one level.

291
00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:07.840
There weren't like multiple steps you had to go up to get to the front door.

292
00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.420
And they had two big doors.

293
00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:11.760
Yeah, for the horse.

294
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.080
For the horse.

295
00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:14.580
All right.

296
00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:17.380
Then he went to Stargate International.

297
00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:19.360
They were our go-to effects company.

298
00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:25.260
He was going to have to create the element of rushing water.

299
00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:30.400
He was going to have to have Dwight on the horse riding into that rushing water.

300
00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:33.740
Dwight bailing off the horse and being rescued.

301
00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:41.900
And then like a series of the horse in various poses to stimulate tumbling down the falls.

302
00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:43.240
Oh, my gosh.

303
00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:52.740
And then Stargate would have to be able to composite all of these and put them behind Jim and Pam in the waterfall as they're getting married.

304
00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.960
Randy said the costs were astronomical.

305
00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:59.840
I was going to say, I think our ending had to have been cheaper.

306
00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:12.540
He said he reached out to Universal Studios back lot because they have a location there called Lower Falls Lake, which is basically that tank that Greg was talking about.

307
00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:13.960
It has an enormous green screen.

308
00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:18.400
It can be filled with warm water to a depth of about eight feet.

309
00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:31.860
But in order to make the water churn, like to simulate the rushing water of the Niagara River, their plan was to chain four jet skis to the side of the tank,

310
00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:36.180
which would then run and create like a whitewater effect.

311
00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.300
So, like, listen to everything.

312
00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.360
He's like, I need four jet ski drivers.

313
00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:46.780
Then he had to contact the animal service company to talk about the horse and get this.

314
00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.140
I did not know this.

315
00:16:48.580 --> 00:17:00.020
Randy learned that you need a special stunt horse because horses actually don't like to walk in water on their own because they don't like to walk or run anywhere where they can't see their hooves.

316
00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:06.620
And he said when you see horses in a Western movie, like dashing across a river, those are specially trained horses.

317
00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:09.240
So they had to, like, start that process immediately.

318
00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.520
Yeah, that makes sense.

319
00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:14.020
So we've got our jet ski drivers.

320
00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.360
We're training the horse to go into water.

321
00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:24.340
But for the digital element of the horse tumbling, he said they were going to have to put a horse into, like,

322
00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:32.980
a green screen harness and then lift the horse on a construction crane against a green screen.

323
00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:43.020
And then have a camera crew, like, shoot, like, 360 degrees around the horse so they could then make it look like it was tumbling.

324
00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:44.680
Like, it would be a visual effect.

325
00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:48.020
They would never tumble the horse, but they do have to suspend the horse.

326
00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.080
Sure, sure, sure.

327
00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:58.320
He said this also required, like, many weeks of training and preparation to make sure that the horse was not stressed, that it was okay being lifted up.

328
00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:09.780
So this whole time, there was a horse actor learning how to get comfortable in water and being suspended in a harness from a crane.

329
00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.340
Yeah, that horse was prepping.

330
00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:12.460
Oh, bless its heart.

331
00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:13.180
Yes.

332
00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:22.980
Then Randy had to find a stunt double for Rain because, obviously, Rain did not want to ride a horse into a tank of rushing water and jump off of it.

333
00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:34.120
So they had to find a special stunt double for Rain, but, he said, they still needed close-ups of Rain's face, so they were going to have to do that facial replacement effect.

334
00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:35.820
Oh, my gosh.

335
00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:39.120
Where they replaced the stuntman's face with Rain's face.

336
00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.420
All right.

337
00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:52.980
In the end, Randy estimated that this two-part episode with the church and the hotel and the Niagara and the cast and the extras and the animals and all the horse stuff,

338
00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:57.460
it was going to be about a million dollars more than our usual budget.

339
00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.120
Oh, my gosh.

340
00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:03.140
And NBC said, you can only have half that.

341
00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:05.700
And he was like, I can't do it all.

342
00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:11.500
Oh, on top of that, I forgot to tell you, Alison Jones told him David Denman is not available.

343
00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:13.020
He's shooting a movie in New Orleans.

344
00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:14.360
They will not let him leave.

345
00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:22.180
So they were also, like, trying to fight with this movie company to get David Denman out for a day so he could ride this horse into the church.

346
00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:27.060
Do you realize how happy Randy was when this gag got pulled?

347
00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:30.320
He must have, like, done a cartwheel down the hallway.

348
00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.580
Like, I can't even imagine.

349
00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:34.180
It did not matter.

350
00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.860
All of the time wasted prepping this.

351
00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:46.800
He was so relieved because he said that freed up the budget so that he could get John and I to Niagara to actually shoot on Maid of the Mist,

352
00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:48.800
which was what he wanted more than anything.

353
00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:56.320
And so he went back to NBC and he said, listen, if you had the budget for this horse business,

354
00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:04.220
you've got the budget to take these two and let them get married as they should on the boat with the real falls behind them.

355
00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:07.820
Oh, so this whole storyline gave him leverage, as it turns out.

356
00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:08.280
Yes!

357
00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:08.880
To NBC.

358
00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:10.380
Completely.

359
00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:16.560
So I hope y'all liked that because I was just like, oh, my gosh.

360
00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:20.140
All this time, all I was doing was, like, trying on different wedding gowns.

361
00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:23.120
And, you know, that was my prep.

362
00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:29.060
It just goes to show how hard our team at the office was always working every week.

363
00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:30.040
Unbelievable.

364
00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:31.760
All right.

